  "content": {
    "prompts": {
      "OVERVIEW": "# Matt Pocock skills — bundled harness\n\nSource: https://github.com/mattpocock/skills (\"Skills for Real Engineers\"). The skills are small and composable; this\nharness chains the engineering ones the way the README describes them.\n\nSkills split by who invokes them. User-invoked skills orchestrate (setup-matt-pocock-skills,\ngrill-with-docs, to-spec, to-tickets, implement, retro); model-invoked skills hold reusable\ndiscipline (grilling, domain-modeling, tdd, codebase-design, diagnosing-bugs, code-review, pr).\nA user-invoked skill may call model-invoked ones, never another user-invoked one.\n\nFlow:\n1. setup-matt-pocock-skills — once per repo: issue tracker, triage labels, docs location.\n2. grill-with-docs — align with the user (grilling) while building the shared language in\n   GLOSSARY.md and ADRs (domain-modeling). The user confirms alignment.\n3. to-spec — publish the spec to the issue tracker.\n4. to-tickets — tracer-bullet tickets with blocking edges.\n5. implement — red-green-refactor via tdd at agreed seams; codebase-design keeps modules deep;\n   diagnosing-bugs for hard bugs.\n6. code-review — two axes, Standards and Spec, as parallel sub-agents. A failing review goes\n   back to implement (folded into the gate so the canvas graph stays acyclic).\n7. pr — PR body with evidence and merge-danger call; a human merges.\n8. retro — environment improvements after the session.\n\nFor large work, `implement-spec` (subagents across the ticket frontier) and `wayfinder`\n(decision-ticket map) replace steps 4–5. Providers are left unset: pick them in the app.\n"
    },
    "agents": {
      "griller": "# grill-with-docs\n\nInterview the user one question at a time until the plan is fully understood. Challenge vague terms against GLOSSARY.md, update it inline, and record hard-to-explain decisions as ADRs.\n",
      "implementer": "# implement\n\nWork the tickets in dependency order. Use red-green-refactor (tdd) at the pre-agreed seams, keep modules deep (codebase-design), and close out with code-review before committing.\n",
      "pr-writer": "# pr\n\nWrite the pull request body: a summary as the smallest visual that makes the change clear, before/after evidence that it works, and a merge-danger call.\n",
      "retro": "# retro\n\nReview the session and suggest improvements to the coding agent's environment, most severe first.\n",
      "setup": "# setup-matt-pocock-skills\n\nConfigure this repo for the engineering skills: ask which issue tracker to use (GitHub, GitLab, local files or other), which labels triage applies, and where docs are saved. Run once per repo.\n",
      "spec-writer": "# to-spec\n\nSynthesize what has already been discussed into a spec and publish it to the configured issue tracker. Ask which modules are touched; do not start a new interview.\n",
      "ticket-writer": "# to-tickets\n\nBreak the spec into thin tracer-bullet tickets that each cut through every layer, and declare each ticket's blocking edges.\n"
    },
    "skills": {
      "code-review": "# code-review\n\nReview the diff since a fixed point on two axes in parallel sub-agents: Standards and Spec. Report them side by side.\n",
      "codebase-design": "# codebase-design\n\nDesign deep modules: a lot of behaviour behind a small interface, placed at a clean seam and tested through that interface.\n",
      "diagnosing-bugs": "# diagnosing-bugs\n\nBuild a feedback loop that goes red on the bug, minimise, hypothesise, instrument, fix, then add a regression test.\n",
      "domain-modeling": "# domain-modeling\n\nBuild and sharpen the project's domain model: challenge terms against the glossary, stress-test with edge cases, update GLOSSARY.md and ADRs.\n",
      "grilling": "# grilling\n\nThe interview primitive: ask relentlessly about a plan, decision or idea until every branch of the design tree is resolved.\n",
      "tdd": "# tdd\n\nRed-green-refactor, one vertical slice at a time: write a failing test, make it pass, then refactor.\n"
    },
    "hooks": {},
    "commands": {
      "grill-with-docs": "Grilling session that also updates GLOSSARY.md and ADRs.",
      "implement": "Build the spec or tickets with tdd and code-review.",
      "retro": "Suggest environment improvements after a session.",
      "setup-matt-pocock-skills": "Configure the repo for the engineering skills.",
      "to-spec": "Publish the current conversation as a spec.",
      "to-tickets": "Split a spec into tracer-bullet tickets."
    },
    "scripts": {}
  },
  "runtime": {
    "preferred": "api",
    "cli": null,
    "env": [],
    "secrets": []
  },
  "validation": {
    "mockProfile": "default"
  }
}
